{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/780429-making-changelings-more-evident-mage-game","id":780429,"title":"Making Changelings more evident (Mage game)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T00:11:50-08:00","id":780429,"title":"Making Changelings more evident (Mage game)","content":"I'm STing a Mage Chronicle, and I'd like to put a couple of changelings in it.<br /> The problem is, it's difficult to make evident that something &quot;fairy&quot; is going on when the Mask is on, and anything you could see is just evident supernatural effects. If I saw the application of the second dot of Contracts of Element (Fire), I would just see someone with fire. Which could be just anything. I could interpret it as a pyrokineticist, or anything else.<br /> How do you suggest allowing mages to get a hint that something &quot;fairy&quot; is going on?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T00:27:20-08:00","id":780431,"title":"","content":"Personify, personify, personify. Describe effects as though they were simple human actors who happen to thematically mesh with the nature of the effects in a manner that suits the context of the scene and/or the fae invoking them.<br /> <br /> Also, allow for a couple of evident instances of catches and pledge-crafting language; weird exchanges of goods and services drive the goblin market in more ways than the weirdly literal, and everything can potentially be communicated with in the context of an offer of boon for task.<br /> <br /> Permit at least a modicum of off-kilter behavior \u2014 a changeling who's accustomed to their state of affairs likely has at least one or two oaths or bargains they're keeping to, and those can be bound to get weird if they're with anything other than a regular human for a minor favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T01:51:27-08:00","id":780453,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, Mage Sight pierces the Mask, doesn't it? And most mages have it up as one of their bread and butter spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:27:45-08:00","id":780516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/780429-making-changelings-more-evident-mage-game?p=780453#post780453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, Mage Sight pierces the Mask, doesn't it? And most mages have it up as one of their bread and butter spells?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, they're not spells any more, according to the 2E development blogs.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> Revelations &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That said, the different flavors to Mage Sight possessed by the Paths means they'll receive different revelations from scrutinizing a Changeling, Hobgoblin, or (Heaven help them) one of the True Fae. Something akin to this tidbit from a Mummy thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/470691-st-spoilers-a-guide-to-mortal-sekhem-sorcerers#post470691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mages who use Active Mage Sight on relics or any mummy is going to gain different information based on their path. </span></span><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Acanthus </span></span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">will be able to see, but not affect, the cosmic fate that binds all Iremite mummes. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moros </span></span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">will be able to see tell that Mummies are undead, and yet have no connection to Stygia or the Ghostly Underworld they are familiar with. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mastigos </span></span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">can see that the minds of the Arisen have been heavily redacted, and they can see that the Deceived minds appear to be splitting into two. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thyrsus </span></span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">can tell little of the Arisen, although they can see where the Shadow is disturbed by the effects of powerful relics upon the populace. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Obrimos </span></span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">mage-sight reveals the power and authority of the Arisen, and Obrimos are the only Mages who can see the celestial hieroglyphics that denote the presence of the Seba. </span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:31:41-08:00","id":780637,"title":"","content":"Ah. Well, in that case, all mages <i>might</i> see signs of a changeling's Kith if it aligns with their Path (such as woodbloods for Thyrsus, gravewights for Moros, most Elementals for Obrimos and slewfeet or riddleseekers for Mastigos), but Acanthus would be the best suited to see any changeling's inherent magicalness. They'd probably see Fate twisting and roiling around changelings like a maelstrom, and they should definitely see Fate shimmering everywhere whenever changelings make Pledges, invoke Contracts or exploit stories in their advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:38:39-08:00","id":781259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/780429-making-changelings-more-evident-mage-game?p=780516#post780516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, they're not spells any more, according to the 2E development blogs.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> Revelations &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That said, the different flavors to Mage Sight possessed by the Paths means they'll receive different revelations from scrutinizing a Changeling, Hobgoblin, or (Heaven help them) one of the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that now <b>Peripherial Mage Sight </b>will &quot;ping&quot; when any fae use Glamour in any way - as using supernatural power.<br /> <br /> <b>Active Mage Sight </b>may point to the weird symbols coming near the changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Focused Mage Sight</b> ( that costs Mana ) I think could just unMask anything fae for the mage. It's literally points to uncover &quot;secret layer of reality&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The next level is <b>Focused Mage Sight</b>, where the mage concentrates her awareness on a particular subject. The hallucinations and sensory artifacts deepen and become more obvious, which mages describe as seeing into the Supernal World. The Obrimos isn\u2019t looking at the world interpreted through the Aether any more, he\u2019s looking at the Aether in the shape of the world \u2014 the walls are straining, barely holding back the power coursing through the cables, strange mandalas are visible in the heart of the sun, and the leader is decked in chains of office. Mana and other sources of magical power are now visible, and the Nimbus of other mages (as well as the mage using Mage Sight) are visible all the time. Supernatural powers including attainments are visible, where only their effects were if covered by the Arcana earlier (for example, a Fire Spirit using its Influence to start a fire will show up under Forces in Active Sight, and both Spirit and Forces in Focused Sight). Clash of Wills rolls to see through concealment effects of the Arcana involved now grant the rote quality to the mage\u2019s roll. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:51:00-08:00","id":781498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/780429-making-changelings-more-evident-mage-game?p=780637#post780637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Well, in that case, all mages <i>might</i> see signs of a changeling's Kith if it aligns with their Path (such as woodbloods for Thyrsus, gravewights for Moros, most Elementals for Obrimos and slewfeet or riddleseekers for Mastigos), but Acanthus would be the best suited to see any changeling's inherent magicalness. They'd probably see Fate twisting and roiling around changelings like a maelstrom, and they should definitely see Fate shimmering everywhere whenever changelings make Pledges, invoke Contracts or exploit stories in their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/780429-making-changelings-more-evident-mage-game?p=781259#post781259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that now <b>Peripherial Mage Sight </b>will &quot;ping&quot; when any fae use Glamour in any way - as using supernatural power.<br /> <br /> <b>Active Mage Sight </b>may point to the weird symbols coming near the changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Focused Mage Sight</b> ( that costs Mana ) I think could just unMask anything fae for the mage. It's literally points to uncover &quot;secret layer of reality&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. These are both pretty logical observations on how Mage Sight works on changelings. I can see <b>Active Mage Sight</b> identifying elements of a changeling's kith if it resonates with the Awakened's Path (as ShadowKnight quoted). For <b>Focused Mage Sight</b>, perhaps it would prompt a Clash of Wills (Gnosis + Arcanum vs Wyrd + Resolve)? I remember Rites of Spring having rules for piercing the Mask, but I can't recall the exact details at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:00:04-08:00","id":781669,"title":"","content":"Well, there is always the obvious Changeling magic in the form of the Hedge and its inhabitants. Remember, everybody can see an open portal into the Hedge. There is no Mask in the Hedge. In other words, observing a careless Changeling enter the Hedge immediately reveal their nature to any observer, sleeper or mage alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}